\alpha_b(\\lambda_b(P))=\\alpha_{16b}(P)$ for every $P\\in E_{16b}(K)$.","route":"../roadmap/model/descent/index.html#isogeny-doubling"},{"id":"model/descent/coordinate-change","title":"The change of variables to $C$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.curveC, ZInQ.theta, ZInQ.theta_some, ZInQ.curveC_two_torsion, ZInQ.two_nsmul_theta_eq_zero_iff, ZInQ.kummer_theta","summary":"Let $\\epsilon=1+s$, $\\delta=3-s$ and $C=E_{-\\delta^2}:y^2=x^3-\\delta^2x$ over $K_0$. Then $\\epsilon^4=17+12s$, $\\epsilon^6=99+70s$, $\\delta=\\epsilon^4d$, and the map is an isomorphism of groups, with inverse $(x,y)\\mapsto(\\epsilon^{-4}x,\\epsilon^{-6}y)$. It maps $E(K_0)[2]$ onto $C(K_0)[2]=\\{O,(0,0),(\\delta,0),(-\\delta,0)\\}$ and satisfies $\\alpha_{-\\delta^2}(\\theta(P))=\\alpha_{-d^2}(P)$ for every $P\\in E(K_0)$.","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"The change of variables to $C$","parts":[["text","The change of variables to "],["math","\\(C\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/model/descent/index.html#coordinate-change"},{"id":"model/descent/point-r-certificate","title":"The certificate for the point $R$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Lemma","lean":"ZInQ.pointR, ZInQ.theta_symm_two_smul_pointR","summary":"In $K_0$, with $\\delta=3-s$:","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"The certificate for the point $R$","parts":[["text","The certificate for the point "],["math","\\(R\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/model/descent/index.html#point-r-certificate"},{"id":"model/descent/first-descent-image","title":"The first descent image has order eight","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.kummer_range_E, ZInQ.card_kummer_range_E, ZInQ.descentGroup_eq","summary":"Let $\\alpha=\\alpha_{-d^2}:E(K_0)\\to K_0^\\times/K_0^{\\times2}$ be the Kummer map of $E$. Its image is the subgroup generated by the classes of $-1$, $\\epsilon=1+s$ and $d$; this subgroup has order $8$, its elements being the classes of $\\pm1,\\pm\\epsilon,\\pm 